Baseline green. Now issue-001.

Slug implementation:

```go
package greeter

import "strings"

// Slug 把一段文本转成 URL 友好的片段：去掉首尾空白，连续空白折成一个连字符，并统一转小写。
func Slug(s string) string {
	return strings.Join(strings.Fields(strings.ToLower(s)), "-")
}
```

Wait: ToLower before Fields is fine. strings.Fields handles all whitespace. "Hello World" -> ["Hello","World"] -> lower -> "hello-world". Good.

Test file slug_test.go with table. Include acceptance cases. Maybe also unicode/extra? Keep minimal per simplicity — cover the three acceptance criteria. I'll add a small table with those three cases plus maybe a tab case? Not requested; keep to acceptance criteria, but a tab/newline case is reasonable given "空白". Simplicity first: just the three.

Actually a table test with the three cases is fine.

Then issue-002:

```go
// JoinSlug 把多个片段各自转成 Slug 后用 "/" 连接，空片段（含纯空白）被跳过。
func JoinSlug(parts ...string) string {
	slugs := make([]string, 0, len(parts))
	for _, p := range parts {
		if s := Slug(p); s != "" {
			slugs = append(slugs, s)
		}
	}
	return strings.Join(slugs, "/")
}
```

Test: JoinSlug("Hello World","Big Day") == "hello-world/big-day"; JoinSlug("a","","b") == "a/b". Also pure whitespace: JoinSlug("a","   ","b") == "a/b" maybe. Acceptance mentions 空串与纯空白. Add that.

